a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(z-6{)}^{2}-{6}^{2}+10\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(z-6{)}^{2}-26.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["213bcf99-b07a-5ff8-9e1b-800ebc1ae1da"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "7e0bb586-f5c8-50a3-a81c-02ec28da37ab" :answer/id #uuid "7e0bb586-f5c8-50a3-a81c-02ec28da37ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=6,\\text{ }q=-27" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6747017d-0da1-56b0-be3e-732f86d538ba" :answer/id #uuid "6747017d-0da1-56b0-be3e-732f86d538ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-6,\\text{ }q=9" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0e0a05d8-a3c3-5e6d-ad81-8ecb0456afe1" :answer/id #uuid "0e0a05d8-a3c3-5e6d-ad81-8ecb0456afe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-12,\\text{ }q=-135" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d5f03c62-5268-52f0-8069-d8b523b26256" :answer/id #uuid "d5f03c62-5268-52f0-8069-d8b523b26256" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-6,\\text{ }q=3" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7ebe950d-cc1e-512a-9f81-12670fd1c22c" :answer/id #uuid "7ebe950d-cc1e-512a-9f81-12670fd1c22c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-6,\\text{ }q=-27" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4ef0ba2d-59d3-5262-8331-20ead9e40170" :answer-field/id #uuid "4ef0ba2d-59d3-5262-8331-20ead9e40170" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["7e0bb586-f5c8-50a3-a81c-02ec28da37ab" "6747017d-0da1-56b0-be3e-732f86d538ba" "0e0a05d8-a3c3-5e6d-ad81-8ecb0456afe1" "d5f03c62-5268-52f0-8069-d8b523b26256" "7ebe950d-cc1e-512a-9f81-12670fd1c22c"] :answer-field/correct "7ebe950d-cc1e-512a-9f81-12670fd1c22c" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "53be2fc6-450b-5f78-baa8-1568c08840a7" :question/id #uuid "53be2fc6-450b-5f78-baa8-1568c08840a7" :question/problem "If the expression ${z}^{2}-12z+9$ is written as $(z+p{)}^{2}+q$, then what are the values of $p$ and $q?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}-2\\cdot 6z+9\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${6}^{2},$ writing the constant term $9$ last:\n\n$$\n{{z}^{2}-2\\cdot 6z+{6}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{6}^{2}+9\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(z-6{)}^{2}-{6}^{2}+9\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(z-6{)}^{2}-27.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-6$ and $q=-27.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["4ef0ba2d-59d3-5262-8331-20ead9e40170"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "ff66e394-5fe8-5f30-959c-f54117e8978f" :answer/id #uuid "ff66e394-5fe8-5f30-959c-f54117e8978f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-4,\\text{ }q=79" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0d071f54-fccc-5708-b874-70a3ee628a4a" :answer/id #uuid "0d071f54-fccc-5708-b874-70a3ee628a4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-2,\\text{ }q=93" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "56d5a1e7-ff71-5591-8a56-2626b93dc60d" :answer/id #uuid "56d5a1e7-ff71-5591-8a56-2626b93dc60d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-2,\\text{ }q=91" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7b98e909-ecee-51dc-8467-4cbed483c0cc" :answer/id #uuid "7b98e909-ecee-51dc-8467-4cbed483c0cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=-2,\\text{ }q=95" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "69a57b48-df2e-5555-9e1e-824807785fa8" :answer/id #uuid "69a57b48-df2e-5555-9e1e-824807785fa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p=2,\\text{ }q=91" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "24591fab-651f-5f9b-bdd0-bb3b130b903f" :answer-field/id #uuid "24591fab-651f-5f9b-bdd0-bb3b130b903f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["ff66e394-5fe8-5f30-959c-f54117e8978f" "0d071f54-fccc-5708-b874-70a3ee628a4a" "56d5a1e7-ff71-5591-8a56-2626b9